Z||000006||horseman||12-15-2000||11:32 PM||||Hey Ross,<BR>Did you check out the link that you provided?<BR>This guy claims to get 335?hp at the rear wheels and 12 and change in the quarter with a turbo 3.2. This is almost unbelievable. He also says that he pulls 1.16 g's on the skidpad. Can anybody verify this? If he is truthful, I want to duplicate it!<P>Charlie||||reg||4
Z||000007||Shaft||12-15-2000||11:40 PM||||Hey OreiF,<P>Just out of curiosity I'd be interested in the info you have about building an IMSA racer||||reg||5
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||12-16-2000||05:30 AM||||Lateral G's over 1 is doable with the right tires and suspension mods (yes even in 84-87 set ups) 335 hp sounds like the full racing engine set up, (even then I would want to see the paperwork before I take anyone's word for it) With such atmospheric boost he would have to have racing fuel. The money and the numbers that he quotes IF they are true means that he probably has an all aluminum Bow Tie Block on it at least. The stock block with that much power would be a ticking time bomb ready to go off. Not likely if it was going to be an uphill racer.<P>The part I thought was interesting is about how the owner didn't want to spend anymore money on the "expensive" SD4 but spent $45,000 dollars on the V6??? <P>Hmmmm...not saying this guy is lying, but maybe the former owner was trying to sweeten the sale...<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000009||Oreif||12-16-2000||10:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaft:<BR><B>Hey OreiF,<P>Just out of curiosity I'd be interested in the info you have about building an IMSA racer</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's in a magazine that has the entire process of building the IMSA race car and includes what parts (and part numbers), blueprints of mounting everything, and mant picture's. I am still scanning in the magazine so I can put it on a CD-ROM. There are a few folks that want a copy. I'm about 2/3's of the way done.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Shaft||12-16-2000||02:29 PM||||Let me know when your done with the CD and how much $$ you want for a copy of it.||||reg||1
